  "accuracyFacts": [
    "SharedArrayBuffer has a standardized Symbol.species accessor, and SharedArrayBuffer.prototype.slice consults it to construct its result; unlike typed-array species, it is an active result-construction hook.",
    "Each concrete TypedArray prototype has a constructor property initially referring to its matching concrete constructor. ArrayBuffer and SharedArrayBuffer prototypes also have constructor and Symbol.toStringTag properties; DataView has a prototype constructor and Symbol.toStringTag.",
    "A DataView constructed over a resizable ArrayBuffer with omitted byteLength is length-tracking; providing byteLength creates a fixed-length view. If a resize makes a fixed view out of bounds, DataView byteLength/byteOffset accessors and reads/writes throw TypeError until the view is back in bounds; an individual access past an in-bounds view range throws RangeError.",
    "TypedArraySpeciesCreate is used by methods such as map, filter, slice, and subarray, whereas ES2023 toReversed, toSorted, and with use TypedArrayCreateSameType and ignore Symbol.species.",
    "The hidden shared %TypedArray%.prototype constructor property refers to the %TypedArray% intrinsic; each concrete typed-array prototype also has its own constructor property pointing to the matching concrete constructor."
  ]
}
